    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1[e]">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Abt">Abt</ref> 1[e]</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1[e]" corresp="#wit-h">Cleroces feoh IIIgylde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#oliver" n="5" corresp="#wit-h">Cleroces feoh III gylde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#oliver" corresp="#wit-h">A cleric’s property [is to be compensated] with 3[-fold] compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">a clerk’s property three fold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-h">a cleric’s property with a three-fold compensation;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Clerikers<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Abt_1-e.lnote.de.8"/> Gut 3fach<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Abt_1-e.lnote.de.9"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">a cleric’s property 3-fold.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Abt_1-e.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">4</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das <hi rend="italic">o</hi> ist durch <hi rend="italic">cliroc, clerochad</hi> bezeugt. — Gemeint ist der Geistliche (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2a) der Weihen vom Kantór bis zum Subdiakon. Er steht hinter Bischof, Priester, Diakon auch Wi 19</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The <hi rend="italic">o</hi> is attested by <hi rend="italic">cliroc, clerochad</hi>. — This means the cleric (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2a) in the orders from cantor to subdeacon. He ranks after bishop, priest and deacon in Wi 19 too</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Abt_1-e.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">4</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dem niederen Kleriker steht der Gemeinfreie gleich in der Ersatzvervielfältigung des ihm Gestohlenen; Abt 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The common freeman ranks equal with the lower cleric in the multiple restitution of what is stolen from him; Abt 9</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
